{
 "duration": 62.291,
 "beats": [
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "What if you breathed air at AQI five hundred, every single day, for one year?",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 4.944
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "Day one. Every breath carries tiny particles called PM two point five. They're small enough to slip deep into your lungs.",
   "start": 5.294,
   "end": 13.107
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "From there, they can enter your bloodstream, and reach every major organ.",
   "start": 13.457,
   "end": 17.894
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "One rough rule of thumb says air this bad is like smoking over ten cigarettes a day. Over a year, that's more than three thousand six hundred.",
   "start": 18.244,
   "end": 26.97
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "The World Health Organization links these particles to stroke, heart disease, lung cancer, and lung disease.",
   "start": 27.32,
   "end": 34.547
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "In a survey of Delhi schoolchildren, forty-three point five percent had reduced lung function, against twenty-five point seven percent in villages.",
   "start": 34.898,
   "end": 43.673
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "And researchers estimate people living in Delhi's average air lose about eight years of life.",
   "start": 44.023,
   "end": 49.694
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "In India alone, air pollution was linked to over one point seven million deaths in twenty twenty-two.",
   "start": 50.044,
   "end": 56.361
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "Clean air isn't a luxury. It's what every breath depends on.",
   "start": 56.711,
   "end": 60.455
  },
  {
   "voice": "michael",
   "text": "Would you move for cleaner air?",
   "start": 60.805,
   "end": 62.291
  }
 ],
